            "Oxidation-reduction reactions transfer electrons: oxidation raises oxidation state, while reduction lowers it. Balance redox equations by conserving atoms, charge, and electrons, including acidic or basic conditions as needed. Analytical methods such as spectroscopy, chromatography, and electrochemistry identify or quantify substances by different physical signals. Good analysis includes calibration, blanks, replicates, uncertainty, and safe handling. A precise number is not automatically an accurate result; evaluate the method and its sources of systematic error.",
